Provenance notice: most prompts (batches 000-021 and 030) are outputs of Anthropic
Claude models generated via the Anthropic API. Use of those outputs must
comply with Anthropic's terms and usage policies (https://www.anthropic.com/legal),
including restrictions on using outputs to train competing models. Batch 037 is the
output of Muse Spark 1.3, a proprietary Meta model accessed through the standard tier
of the Meta Model API (https://developer.meta.com/ai/products/meta-model-api/) via
OpenRouter; use of those prompts must comply with Meta's terms for that API. Batches
022-029, 031, and 040 were generated with Qwen 3.8 27B (open weights, Apache 2.0), and, via OpenRouter,
batches 032-033 with DeepSeek V4 Pro and batches 039 and 041 with DeepSeek V4.1 Flash
(both open weights, MIT) and batches 034-035 with GLM-5.3
(open weights, GLM-5.3 License: MIT terms plus a security-review condition for
model-as-a-service operators above 10 billion US dollars in annual revenue; no
restrictions on the use of outputs), and batches 036 and 038 with Qwen3.8 2.4T-A95B (open
weights, Qwen3.8-Max License: MIT terms plus an attribution requirement above 100
million monthly users or 20 million US dollars in monthly revenue, and a separate
license for model-as-a-service businesses above 50 million US dollars in annual
revenue; no restrictions on the use of outputs). The
generating model for every individual prompt is recorded in its .meta.yaml
sidecar. Responses under responses/ are outputs of open-weights models whose
licenses (Apache 2.0, MIT) place no restrictions on the use of outputs; the
model is named in every record and in each run's run.yaml. A response record
also contains the prompt it answers, so records answering Claude-written
prompts carry the notice above with them. Preference judgments under preferences/
(the verdict, the judge's visible reasoning, and its summarized thinking) are
outputs of Anthropic Claude models generated via the Anthropic API and carry the
notice above; the judge model is named in every record and in each run's run.yaml.
In addition, a small number of prompts across all batches were
emended during curation by a Claude model, so an emended prompt may contain
Claude-written text regardless of which model its sidecar names. Prompts may include brief quotations from published works and
translations, reproduced for purposes of commentary and analysis; such
quotations remain the property of their respective rights holders.
